{{!-- What this watch looks like: the sky over it, who is walking under it, and what the party
      does with it. Three headings, one per question, each with its own drawn rule.

      The weather is a segmented control rather than a combobox — six rows plus Auto is a closed
      range, and a run shows the whole Difficulty scale with today marked on it, which a dropdown
      hides behind a click. Auto is the empty value: it hands the day back to the dice, which is
      also what every new day does on its own. Each button's row of the table is its tooltip
      rather than a line of prose under the run: the run is seven buttons wide and needs the whole
      band to stay on one line, and a sentence that changes length under it moved everything
      below by however long today's reading happened to be.

      The heading carries the three watches of the day at its right, because the sky is the sky
      OF a watch — the day's number is up in the header with the route.

      The party's own rolls sit under THEIR heading, not under the action's: the SRD hands both to
      the table rather than the Warden ("The party rolls 1d6 to see if they get lost"; "One or
      more party members may hunt, fish, or forage"). They are also the buttons that come and go,
      and under the action they pushed the watch's one button down a row every time one appeared.

      A roster row reads left to right in one direction: who they are, a drawn rule, then what
      they are carrying into the night — Rations left, Fatigue carried, and Deprived, which is
      what decides whether tonight's camp restores anything. At the far right, for the Warden,
      the one control: take them off this journey.

      The list IS who is travelling, and it is dropped into rather than derived — the SRD charges
      "each party member (and their mounts)", so a mount and a hired guide belong on it and no
      rule about players or ownership can put them there. Drag a party onto the list and its
      members arrive at once; drag one Actor and it arrives alone.

      A player sees every control set and none of them movable, and keeps the party's two rolls,
      which the SRD hands the table rather than the Warden. --}}
<section class="cairn-journey-watch">
{{#if journey}}
    <h3 class="cairn-edit-group cairn-journey-heading" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="journey-weather"
        data-ink-w="1.8" data-ink-at="bottom">
        <span>{{localize "CAIRN.Journey.Weather"}}</span>
        <ol class="cairn-journey-watches">
            {{#each watches}}<li class="{{#if current}}current{{/if}}">{{label}}</li>{{/each}}
        </ol>
    </h3>

    <div class="cairn-choice cairn-journey-weather" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.Journey.SetWeather'}}">
        {{#each weathers as |w|}}
        <label class="cairn-choice-option" data-tooltip-text="{{w.effect}}">
            <input type="radio" name="weather" value="{{w.key}}" data-action="setWeather"
                   {{checked w.selected}} {{disabled (not ../isGM)}} />
            <span>{{w.label}}</span>
        </label>
        {{/each}}
    </div>

    {{!-- The table says "or", so the Warden chooses which toll the weather takes. --}}
    {{#if isGM}}
    {{#if weather}}
    <div class="cairn-journey-weather-toll">
        {{#if weather.fatigue}}<button type="button" data-action="addFatigue"><i class="fas fa-weight-hanging" inert></i> {{localize "CAIRN.Journey.AddFatigue"}}</button>{{/if}}
        {{#if weather.watch}}<button type="button" data-action="adjust" data-field="watchesNeeded" data-delta="1"><i class="fas fa-plus" inert></i> {{localize "CAIRN.Journey.AddWatch"}}</button>{{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}
    {{/if}}

    <h3 class="cairn-edit-group cairn-journey-heading" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="journey-party"
        data-ink-w="1.8" data-ink-at="bottom">{{localize "CAIRN.Journey.PartyHeading"}}</h3>

    {{#if need.lost}}
    <button type="button" class="cairn-journey-roll" data-action="rollLost">
        <i class="fas fa-compass" inert></i> {{localize "CAIRN.Journey.RollLost" odds=route.lostOdds}}
    </button>
    {{/if}}
    {{!-- Supply has two answers and the SRD gives both: forage for a rolled bounty, or "encounter
          homes and small villages, spending gold and a full watch to resupply". One watch, two
          ways to take it — the same shape the weather's "or" wears above. --}}
    {{#if need.supply}}
    <div class="cairn-journey-supply">
        <button type="button" data-action="rollSupply">
            <i class="fas fa-leaf" inert></i> {{localize "CAIRN.Journey.RollSupply"}}
        </button>
        <button type="button" data-action="resupply">
            <i class="fas fa-house-chimney" inert></i> {{localize "CAIRN.Journey.Resupply"}}
        </button>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    <ul class="cairn-plain-list cairn-journey-crew">
        {{#each party as |pc|}}
        <li class="cairn-slot cairn-journey-member" data-actor-id="{{pc.id}}" data-actor-uuid="{{pc.uuid}}"
            {{#unless @last}}data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="journey-member-{{pc.id}}" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-at="bottom"{{/unless}}>
            <button type="button" class="cairn-journey-who" data-action="openSheet" data-actor-id="{{pc.id}}"
                    aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.Journey.OpenSheet' name=pc.name}}">
                <img class="cairn-journey-portrait" src="{{pc.img}}" alt="" />
                <span class="cairn-journey-name">{{pc.name}}</span>
            </button>
            {{!-- Paints nothing: an empty span the ink layer strokes a vline over, the way the
                  Fatigue track's rule is drawn. --}}
            <span class="cairn-journey-divide" data-ink="vline" data-ink-seed="journey-divide-{{pc.id}}"
                  data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42"></span>
            <span class="cairn-journey-load">
                <span class="cairn-item-tag" data-tooltip-text="{{localize 'CAIRN.Journey.Rations'}}">
                    <i class="fas fa-drumstick-bite" inert></i> {{pc.rations}}
                </span>
                <span class="cairn-item-tag" data-tooltip-text="{{localize 'CAIRN.Journey.Fatigue'}}">
                    <i class="fas fa-weight-hanging" inert></i> {{pc.fatigue}}
                </span>
                {{#if pc.deprived}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{localize "CAIRN.Condition.Deprived"}}</span>{{/if}}
            </span>
            {{!-- Primitive 7's control cell, the same one every other list row in the system
                  wears. `{{#each}}` swaps the context for the row, so the Warden flag is one
                  frame up. --}}
            {{#if ../isGM}}
            <span class="cairn-item-controls">
                <a data-action="removeCrew" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.Journey.RemoveCrew'}}"><i class="fas fa-xmark"></i></a>
            </span>
            {{/if}}
        </li>
        {{else}}
        <li class="cairn-journey-member cairn-journey-empty">{{localize "CAIRN.Journey.DropCrew"}}</li>
        {{/each}}
    </ul>

    <h3 class="cairn-edit-group cairn-journey-heading" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="journey-action"
        data-ink-w="1.8" data-ink-at="bottom">{{localize "CAIRN.Journey.Action"}}</h3>

    {{!-- One row: the closed list of four, and the button that spends the watch on whichever is
          chosen. Nothing else — a roll the watch owes belongs to whoever owes it, above. --}}
    <div class="cairn-journey-take">
        <div class="cairn-choice cairn-journey-action" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.Journey.Action'}}">
            {{#each actions as |a|}}
            <label class="cairn-choice-option">
                <input type="radio" name="action" value="{{a.key}}" data-action="setAction"
                       {{checked a.selected}} {{disabled (not ../isGM)}} />
                <span>{{a.label}}</span>
            </label>
            {{/each}}
        </div>
        {{!-- The reading goes on the WRAPPER, not the button: a disabled button raises no pointer
              event of its own, and core reads the tooltip from the element the pointer enters
              (the same rule the toggle partial spells out). On the wrapper it is reachable in
              both states, and it says what the watch still owes while the button is dead. --}}
        {{#if isGM}}
        <span class="cairn-journey-resolve-wrap" data-tooltip-text="{{resolveHint}}">
            <button type="button" class="cairn-journey-resolve" data-action="resolveWatch" {{disabled (not canResolve)}}>
                <i class="fas fa-hourglass-end" inert></i> {{localize "CAIRN.Journey.Resolve"}}
            </button>
        </span>
        {{/if}}
    </div>
{{/if}}
</section>
